{
	title: 'A message sent mid-turn never reads as a cancel',
	spec: "When a user message interrupts a turn (task 8p), any tool call it stops or keeps from running says so in its result: 'interrupted by a new user message, which follows; nothing was canceled: read it, then carry on'. The model must read that the user spoke and carry on with its work after answering, never that the user wanted the work canceled. Escape, a pause by Hal, a close or another real stop says 'canceled (the next hal-note says why)' (not started) or 'stopped (the next hal-note says why)' (killed): the turn-end note names who paused and why. A /stop of one call, which leaves the turn running and adds no note, aborts with the string reason 'by the user', and the result says so. This holds for a command waiting on another tab's declared files, one about to launch, one running, and calls not yet dispatched. The steer aborts with the reason jobs.steered; jobs.why(signal) words it.",
	status: 'done',
	notes: [
		"Invariant restored: a steer is never reported to the model as a cancel. Before, every abort said 'canceled; the command did not run', and the model told the user it had been canceled and stopped working.",
		"Invariant restored: a stop's tool result never names the wrong cause. Before, every non-steer abort said 'canceled by the user', even when Hal paused the turn, and the model read a user pause as a rejection."
	],
	needs: ['8p'],
	foldInto: ['8p']
}
